<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Custom on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/custom/</link><description>Recent content in Custom on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 20 Dec 2016 09:03:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/custom/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Building Raspberry PI image using Vagrant</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/building-raspberry-pi-image-using/</link><pubDate>Tue, 20 Dec 2016 09:03:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/building-raspberry-pi-image-using/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Building your own Raspberry Pi Images&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjVG_n8KUxrSA1GvKJRMktj_YDDC5AHFZ331zBaaRvndeaL6TtDnlsnPc-PzYYKhlRDipiBQvBFsfJku0GmF6Quqc_tE25IJX-4UtOBXWcmijnFdGET-vV7rvfSotDRH5Ea5boHEvBFAqQ/s1600/raspberrypi2.jpg" imageanchor="1" style="margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"&gt;&lt;img border="0" height="181" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjVG_n8KUxrSA1GvKJRMktj_YDDC5AHFZ331zBaaRvndeaL6TtDnlsnPc-PzYYKhlRDipiBQvBFsfJku0GmF6Quqc_tE25IJX-4UtOBXWcmijnFdGET-vV7rvfSotDRH5Ea5boHEvBFAqQ/s320/raspberrypi2.jpg" width="320" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;The Vagrant file on &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/pibuild"&gt;https://github.com/alastairhm/pibuild&lt;/a&gt; sets up a build environment for building Raspberry Pi images from the repository &lt;a href="https://github.com/RPi-Distro/pi-gen"&gt;https://github.com/RPi-Distro/pi-gen&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;I am using it to create a custom image minimal with &lt;a href="https://www.docker.com/"&gt;Docker&lt;/a&gt; pre-installed based on &lt;a href="https://github.com/jonasrosland/pi-gen"&gt;https://github.com/jonasrosland/pi-gen&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;although you can edit the scripts to pre-install the packages you want in your image.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>